[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application processes user-supplied regex patterns without adequate validation or restrictions, allowing an attacker to craft complex regex patterns that can cause excessive backtracking and significantly degrade the performance of the server. If the application directly uses these patterns to search through file contents, it may lead to resource exhaustion, making the service unresponsive or crashing it altogether. This type of vulnerability is particularly concerning in applications that handle regex inputs from users, as it can be exploited to disrupt service availability.

